1
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:11,200
The American Red Cross on Naval Station Guantanamo Bay held

2
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,560
a hurricane preparedness event featuring base organizations such as Fleet

3
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:17,905
and Family, the fire department, and security, who provided information

4
00:00:17,905 --> 00:00:19,665
on tropical weather emergencies.

5
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:23,985
The important reason why we have this preparedness event is

6
00:00:23,985 --> 00:00:27,665
to make sure our community is resilient and can respond

7
00:00:27,665 --> 00:00:31,210
and recover from disasters that happen.

8
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:33,850
We want to make sure that their families are prepared if

9
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:36,650
they have to evacuate or if they have to go

10
00:00:36,650 --> 00:00:37,850
into shelters.

11
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:41,930
Naval Station Guantanamo Bay is in a very unique

12
00:00:41,930 --> 00:00:42,570
position.

13
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:45,345
We are in the path of many of the hurricanes

14
00:00:45,345 --> 00:00:46,465
that come through.

15
00:00:46,705 --> 00:00:49,505
So we need to be prepared in order to meet

16
00:00:49,505 --> 00:00:51,985
those challenges that those hurricanes bring.

17
00:00:53,025 --> 00:00:56,065
Reporting from AFN Guantanamo Bay, I'm Petty Officer Zach Guth.
